            <creation xml:id="creation_214N20134">
               <date isodate="1831" xml:id="date_N20386">1831</date>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_214N20132">
               <p xml:id="idm87">Dating according to Alfred Nielsen. The cantata was probably composed for Crown Prince Christian (the later King Christian VIII) whom Hartmann had known since his childhood. From 1827 to 1843 Hartmann was a teacher at Giusppe Siboni's academy of music, in which Christian as a crown prince took a keen interest. When he was crowned King of Denmark in 1840, he presented Hartmann with the a Knight's Cross as an appreciation of his work at the academy.</p>
            </history>
